{"name":"Blue Exult","hex":"#2b2f43","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"exult","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To rejoice; to be very happy, especially in triumph; to triumph (over)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exult"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ultima VII: The Black Gate","blocks":[{"text":"Ultima VII: The Black Gate is the seventh installment of the Ultima series of role-playing video games. It was published in April 1992 for MS-DOS by Origin Systems. The player returns as The Avatar, a would-be paragon of moral virtue who faces down many dangers and deceptions in order to cleanse the medieval fantasy world of Britannia of assorted plots and schemes, monster infestations, and the undermining of crown authority. A Super NES conversion was released in 1994."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b3/Ultima_VII_Black_Gate_box.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ultima_VII%3A_The_Black_Gate"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d7/Ultima7-bg-exult.png/250px-Ultima7-bg-exult.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d7/Ultima7-bg-exult.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d7/Ultima7-bg-exult.png/250px-Ultima7-bg-exult.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dialogue in Ultima VII, taken in Exult","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUltima7-bg-exult.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c9/Ultima_7_-_Forge_Of_Virtue_box_cover.jpg/250px-Ultima_7_-_Forge_Of_Virtue_box_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c9/Ultima_7_-_Forge_Of_Virtue_box_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c9/Ultima_7_-_Forge_Of_Virtue_box_cover.jpg/250px-Ultima_7_-_Forge_Of_Virtue_box_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Box cover for Ultima VII: Forge of Virtue expansion, depicting The Black Sword","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUltima_7_-_Forge_Of_Virtue_box_cover.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/2010._%D0%94%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B5%D1%86%D0%BA._%D0%9A%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%BD%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B0%D0%BB_%